    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-rĭgesco</span></b> ,
			gŭi, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i> (occurring only in the
				<i>perf.</i>), <i>to become
			stiff</i> or <i>rigid; to curdle</i> (a <b>poet.</b> word): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formidine sanguis deriguit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 260</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deriguere oculi,</span>”
				<i>were fixed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 7, 447</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 754</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hirsutae comae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					3, 332</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					3, 613</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cervix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 233</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Niobe malis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 6, 303</span></i>
			 (al. diriguit).</div>
